# Search Prior Teachings

When the user asks what has already been taught, or when drafting/brainstorming/editing a sermon or lesson that overlaps an existing theme, scripture, series, or tag:

1. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/search-teachings/SKILL.md`
2. Run the local search CLI from the repo root as that skill specifies
3. Ground answers only in real CLI hits — do not invent matches

## Clickable Results (Required)

Whenever you list search hits or cite prior teachings, every file must be a **markdown link with an absolute workspace path**.

```markdown
- [Walking in the Spirit](/Users/jameslamar/james-obsidian-sync/Personal/teachings/sermons/2025-09-06-walking-in-the-spirit.md) — Freedom from religious requirements (score 0.72)
```

### Format rules

- Link text: short human title (from frontmatter `title` or the filename slug)
- Link target: absolute path under this workspace (must start with `/Users/...`)
- Filenames use hyphens (`YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`) — no spaces
- Optional: one-line why it matched (snippet theme, series, or score)
- Prefer a compact list of unique files over dumping every chunk hit
- Do **not** use code-citation fences (`` ```1:1:path ``) for result lists — they do not open reliably in this workspace
- Do **not** wrap paths only in backticks

### Bad

````markdown
- `sermons/2025-09-06-walking-in-the-spirit.md`
- ```1:1:sermons/2025-09-06-walking-in-the-spirit.md```
- [Walking in the Spirit](sermons/2025-09-06-walking-in-the-spirit.md)
````

### Good

```markdown
- [Walking in the Spirit](/Users/jameslamar/james-obsidian-sync/Personal/teachings/sermons/2025-09-06-walking-in-the-spirit.md)
```
